WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.982
This query creates an illustrative score out of four component checks.

00:00:03.982 --> 00:00:09.287
Each contributes twenty-five points. That weighting is a policy choice for teaching.

00:00:09.287 --> 00:00:12.727
Another organization might value the dimensions differently.

00:00:12.727 --> 00:00:19.602
The important lesson is to keep the component checks visible and avoid treating a composite score as an

00:00:19.602 --> 00:00:24.157
objective truth. Validation is rule-based detection, not automatic correction.

00:00:24.157 --> 00:00:30.297
A failed email-shape check tells you that a record deserves attention; it does not tell you the correct email.

00:00:30.297 --> 00:00:36.230
Treat quality flags as evidence that can drive quarantine, review, or a documented repair process.
